"""Office explanations: reviewed institutions, contextual job families and explicit authority limits.

Directory records establish a listing, not a personal delegation. General profiles are
labelled as such; institutional functions are never inherited as a staff member's powers.
"""
import re
from collections import Counter

CONSTITUTION='https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/19150/1/constitution_of_india.pdf'
PROFILES={}
def profile(key,description,actions,limits,example,reference=None):
    PROFILES[key]={'description':description,'actions':actions.split('|'),'limits':limits.split('|'),'example':example,'reference':reference}

# Functional institution profiles. These describe the body, not each person in its directory.
profile('agriculture','Organises field support for crop cultivation and implementation of agricultural programmes. Extension staff translate farming advice and scheme rules into services for growers.', 'Organise farmer training and field demonstrations|Coordinate delivery of approved agricultural assistance|Monitor crop conditions and submit programme reports', 'Assistance depends on scheme eligibility, budget and the competent sanctioning officer.', 'A crop problem can lead to a field visit, technical advice and referral to an eligible support programme.')
profile('horticulture','Supports fruit, vegetable, flower and plantation-crop development, including better planting material and cultivation practices.', 'Arrange horticultural extension and technical guidance|Process eligible applications under horticulture programmes|Monitor nurseries and supported cultivation projects within its remit','It does not guarantee a crop price or approve every agricultural subsidy.','A grower seeking to establish an orchard may receive technical guidance and assistance under an available scheme.')
profile('cooperation','Administers the legal and institutional framework for co-operative societies. Regulatory work and member-service work are distinct from commercial banking.', 'Process society registration and by-law matters where authorised|Arrange statutory audit, inspection or inquiry under applicable provisions|Examine governance and compliance matters within the office’s jurisdiction','A society’s registrar does not automatically decide every contractual dispute; statutory appeal and tribunal routes remain applicable.','A society’s governance complaint may be examined against its by-laws and the relevant co-operative law.')
profile('cooperative-bank','Provides banking and credit services through the co-operative banking network, including agricultural and other eligible lending.', 'Appraise loan applications against lending rules|Disburse sanctioned credit and manage repayment|Provide the banking products offered by the institution','Credit requires eligibility, appraisal and sanction; government association does not make a loan an automatic entitlement.','A co-operative institution may seek seasonal credit through the bank’s approved lending arrangements.')
profile('seeds','Supports the availability and supply of seed for cultivation. Procurement, processing, quality arrangements and distribution are operational responsibilities of the seed institution.', 'Plan seed procurement or production programmes|Arrange processing, storage and distribution of available seed|Monitor supply and coordinate with agriculture field offices','Seed distribution does not itself certify every private seed product or guarantee yield.','Before a sowing season, seed stocks can be prepared and supplied through approved channels.')
profile('seed-certification','Examines seed-production and certification work against the standards applicable to the certification programme.', 'Receive certification applications and inspect eligible seed production|Arrange sampling, testing and certification decisions through authorised processes|Maintain certification records and compliance follow-up','Certification applies to the inspected product and scheme; it is not a blanket guarantee of farm performance.','A seed producer applies for certification and the crop and seed lot are assessed against prescribed requirements.')
profile('marketing','Supports organised agricultural markets and marketing facilities so farm produce can move through established trading channels.', 'Coordinate market infrastructure and market services|Monitor market administration within the allocated jurisdiction|Implement approved marketing-support measures','It does not independently promise a minimum support price or purchase every crop.','A market-yard infrastructure issue can be reviewed and a sanctioned improvement proposed.')
profile('warehousing','Provides storage and associated handling services for agricultural and other permitted commodities.', 'Operate storage facilities and accept eligible goods under service terms|Arrange handling and preservation procedures|Maintain stock and warehouse documentation','Storage receipts and services are governed by the applicable contract and regulatory requirements.','A depositor can store an accepted commodity and obtain the documentation applicable to that warehouse service.')
profile('animal-health','Coordinates veterinary care, livestock disease prevention and animal-husbandry development services.', 'Organise veterinary treatment and vaccination programmes|Coordinate disease surveillance and field reporting|Implement approved livestock-development support','Treatment and assistance are delivered through authorised veterinary staff and scheme-specific arrangements.','Reports of animal disease can trigger veterinary examination and an appropriate disease-control response.')
profile('fisheries','Develops inland fisheries and supports fishers and fishery institutions through approved programmes and technical services.', 'Provide fisheries extension and technical guidance|Implement eligible fishery-development measures|Coordinate stocking and development work where assigned','Water-body rights, leases and assistance follow the relevant rules and competent authority.','A fishers’ group may seek advice and eligible programme support for a permitted fishery activity.')
profile('dairy','Supports dairy co-operatives and milk procurement, processing and marketing through its operational network.', 'Arrange milk collection and quality checks|Operate or coordinate processing and marketing|Provide member services and approved producer support','Purchase terms and producer assistance depend on the federation’s current arrangements.','Milk from a participating producer is collected, tested and routed into the federation’s processing chain.')
profile('university','Provides higher education, research and academic development in its assigned disciplines. Academic governance and the administration of affiliated institutions follow the university’s legal framework.', 'Run approved courses, examinations and research programmes|Award qualifications through the prescribed academic process|Administer admissions and institutional matters under applicable rules','Admission, affiliation and academic decisions require the competent university or regulatory authority.','A student enters an approved programme, completes assessment and receives a qualification after meeting its requirements.')
profile('welfare-finance','Implements approved financial-development support for its named community or beneficiary group. Support may involve loans, subsidy-linked assistance, training or coordination with banks.', 'Invite and examine applications under an announced programme|Recommend or sanction eligible assistance within delegated limits|Monitor supported activities and programme expenditure','There is no automatic entitlement to a loan, subsidy or job; current scheme rules and funding apply.','An eligible applicant’s livelihood proposal can be appraised and routed for the assistance available under a current programme.')
profile('residential-education','Operates a network of residential educational institutions for the group identified in its mandate, combining teaching with hostel and student-welfare administration.', 'Administer admissions under published eligibility rules|Manage school or college teaching and residential facilities|Monitor academic progress, staffing and student welfare','Admission and benefits depend on the institution’s current prospectus and rules.','A selected student receives education and residential support at an institution in the society’s network.')
profile('study-circle','Provides examination coaching and related preparation support for eligible learners under its approved programmes.', 'Announce available coaching batches and eligibility|Select candidates and organise teaching and practice assessments|Monitor attendance and learning support','Coaching does not confer a government appointment or guarantee selection in an examination.','An eligible candidate can apply to an announced competitive-examination coaching batch.')
profile('civil-supplies','Coordinates the movement and distribution of foodgrain and essential commodities through the public-distribution and food-security system.', 'Plan procurement, storage or movement of assigned foodgrain|Coordinate supply to authorised distribution channels|Monitor stock movement and programme delivery','Ration eligibility and any procurement entitlement follow current government rules.','A supply shortage can be checked against stock records and escalated for replenishment through the distribution network.')
profile('legal-metrology','Administers measurement standards and consumer protections relating to weights, measures and regulated packaged commodities.', 'Inspect and verify regulated weights and measures through authorised officers|Examine complaints about short measurement or package declarations|Take compliance action permitted by legal-metrology law','Inspection, seizure or prosecution must follow the statutory procedure and an officer’s authorisation.','A complaint about an inaccurate shop scale can be assessed by an authorised metrology officer.')
profile('consumer-commission','Adjudicates consumer disputes within the jurisdiction given to the commission by consumer-protection law.', 'Hear admissible consumer complaints and appeals|Examine evidence and conduct proceedings|Order remedies provided by law in a decided case','Monetary, territorial and subject-matter jurisdiction determine the appropriate forum; filing does not guarantee relief.','A qualifying complaint about a deficient service can be heard and decided by the competent consumer commission.')
profile('electricity-regulator','Regulates the electricity sector within the state under the Electricity Act. Its regulatory role is distinct from operating a power plant or repairing a local supply line.', 'Determine regulated tariffs through the prescribed proceedings|Consider licences and electricity-procurement matters within its remit|Hear matters and issue regulatory orders within statutory jurisdiction','It must act through the applicable law, procedure and appeal framework; a distribution utility handles day-to-day supply service.','A utility’s tariff proposal is examined in a regulatory proceeding before an applicable tariff order is issued.','https://tgerc.telangana.gov.in/aboutus.php')
profile('power-generation','Operates or develops electricity-generating assets and manages generation-related engineering, fuel and plant operations.', 'Schedule and operate available generating units in coordination with the grid|Procure plant services and maintain equipment under approved procedures|Plan generation projects for the necessary approvals','It does not independently set retail electricity tariffs or issue household supply connections.','A generating unit is taken through planned maintenance so it can return to service safely.')
profile('power-transmission','Transports electricity through the state’s high-voltage network and maintains the infrastructure used for bulk power movement.', 'Operate and maintain transmission lines and substations|Plan network strengthening and execute sanctioned works|Coordinate outages and network operations with the relevant grid authorities','Its network role is different from a distribution company’s retail billing and service connections.','A new substation proposal is technically examined and implemented after the required approvals.')
profile('power-distribution','Delivers electricity to consumers through the local distribution network and administers supply connections, metering and billing.', 'Process eligible connection and load-change applications|Maintain distribution equipment and respond to supply faults|Issue bills and handle service complaints under the applicable standards','Tariffs and supply conditions follow regulatory orders; individual officers act within delegated authority.','A consumer reports an outage and the distribution utility identifies the affected feeder and arranges a repair.')
profile('renewable-energy','Facilitates renewable-energy and energy-conservation programmes and helps implement approved clean-energy initiatives.', 'Provide programme information and technical facilitation|Coordinate eligible renewable-energy projects and assistance|Monitor projects and conservation activities assigned to it','Grid connectivity, tariff and subsidy approvals may require separate competent authorities.','A rooftop-solar proposal can be guided to the programme and utility approvals relevant to the installation.')
profile('mineral-enterprise','Undertakes mining or mineral-development activities allotted to the enterprise and manages associated projects and commercial operations.', 'Plan permitted extraction and mineral-development projects|Operate approved activities and manage sale arrangements|Arrange safety, environmental and contractual compliance','The enterprise still requires the applicable mining rights, clearances and operating permissions.','A permitted mineral project progresses through planning, approvals and compliant operations.')
profile('electrical-inspection','Carries out electrical-safety inspection and related statutory administration through authorised technical officers.', 'Inspect installations falling within its statutory jurisdiction|Examine compliance and accident-related technical information|Issue approvals or directions only where the law and delegation authorise','It is not the power distributor and does not resolve every billing complaint.','An installation requiring statutory inspection is examined before the prescribed approval can be considered.')
profile('forest','Manages assigned forests and undertakes conservation, protection and forestry programmes through field and technical staff.', 'Prepare and implement approved forest-management work|Carry out protection and enforcement through authorised officers|Coordinate restoration, plantations and wildlife-related work within the assigned charge','Forest diversion, wildlife permissions and enforcement powers depend on the relevant law and competent authority.','A report of illegal felling can be inspected and acted on through the authorised forest-enforcement process.')
profile('pollution-control','Administers environmental consents, monitoring and pollution-control enforcement within the board’s statutory remit.', 'Assess consent applications and compliance reports|Inspect and sample through authorised procedures|Issue statutory directions or initiate proceedings where empowered','Each action requires the relevant environmental law and procedure; it is not a general municipal-sanitation office.','An industrial pollution complaint may lead to inspection, sampling and a compliance decision.')
profile('biodiversity','Supports conservation and sustainable use of biodiversity and administration of the state-level functions allocated under biodiversity law.', 'Coordinate biodiversity-management institutions and documentation|Examine matters referred under the applicable biodiversity framework|Promote conservation awareness and technical support','Access permissions and benefit-sharing decisions depend on the relevant authority and law.','A local biodiversity inventory can be supported through the relevant biodiversity-management committee.')
profile('research-training','Builds knowledge and professional capacity in its named field through research, training and technical support.', 'Design and deliver relevant training programmes|Carry out or commission studies and technical assessments|Publish findings and support participating departments','Training or a research recommendation does not itself grant regulatory or sanctioning authority.','A department can use a training programme or a technical study to improve how its staff handle an assigned function.')
profile('zoo','Maintains a zoological collection, animal care and visitor facilities while supporting conservation education.', 'Provide animal care and manage enclosures|Operate public visits and education programmes|Coordinate conservation and veterinary work under the applicable standards','Wildlife handling and transfers require the prescribed permissions.','A veterinary and animal-care team plans treatment and enclosure management for an animal in its care.')
profile('treasury','Processes government financial transactions and maintains treasury accounts within the applicable treasury and financial rules.', 'Scrutinise bills and payment authorisations submitted through the system|Record receipts, payments and reconciliations|Process authorised pension or other treasury transactions as allocated','It cannot create a spending sanction or release money solely because a claim has been submitted.','A sanctioned departmental bill is checked for the required authority and accounting classification before payment processing.')
profile('audit','Examines the accounts and financial compliance of the institutions assigned to the audit organisation.', 'Inspect records and check transactions against applicable rules|Report irregularities and seek explanations|Follow up on audit observations and corrective responses','An audit observation is not by itself a criminal conviction or a final recovery order.','An unsupported expense may be recorded in an audit report and referred to the institution for an explanation and corrective action.')
profile('government-insurance','Administers the government-insurance arrangements assigned to the department, including policy records and eligible claims.', 'Maintain policy and subscription records|Process eligible policy services and claims|Check documents and authorise transactions within delegation','Benefits depend on the policy, eligibility and applicable scheme rules.','An employee’s policy claim is checked against service and subscription records before a decision under the scheme.')
profile('pension','Administers the pension-payment work allocated to the office and maintains the records needed for authorised payments.', 'Verify pension-payment authorisations and supporting records|Process eligible pension payments and revisions within its remit|Resolve payment-record discrepancies with the sanctioning authority','The payment office does not independently create a pension entitlement or amend service rules.','A pensioner’s payment discrepancy can be checked against the pension-payment order and transaction records.')
profile('government-residency','Represents and supports the state government’s assigned coordination, liaison and official accommodation functions outside the state Secretariat.', 'Liaise with the relevant governments and institutions|Coordinate official visits and assigned accommodation services|Process correspondence and matters referred to the residency','A liaison office does not acquire the statutory powers of the department with which it coordinates.','A state delegation’s official visit can be supported through liaison and accommodation arrangements.')
profile('public-health','Coordinates population-level health programmes, disease prevention and the field public-health network within its charge.', 'Monitor disease reports and organise prevention measures|Coordinate public-health campaigns and field health services|Review programme performance and respond through authorised health teams','Clinical treatment and statutory public-health orders are issued by the appropriate authorised professionals and authorities.','An increase in reported infections can trigger surveillance review and a targeted public-health response.')
profile('hospital-administration','Administers the hospital network or health services assigned to the institution, including service capacity and operational support.', 'Coordinate hospital staffing, facilities and service delivery|Monitor supplies and operational requirements|Review performance and refer clinical matters to qualified teams','Administrative leadership does not replace clinical judgement or licensing requirements.','A hospital’s equipment shortage can be assessed and taken through an approved procurement or allocation process.')
profile('medical-education','Coordinates medical teaching institutions, training and the services administered through the medical-education network.', 'Administer assigned medical colleges and teaching hospitals|Coordinate academic and training arrangements with competent bodies|Monitor institutional capacity and approved development works','Professional recognition, admissions and clinical decisions follow the relevant regulatory and institutional rules.','A teaching institution’s capacity requirement can be reviewed and proposed for the appropriate academic and administrative approvals.')
profile('drugs-control','Regulates the manufacture and sale of medicines and other products within the Drugs Control Administration’s statutory jurisdiction.', 'Inspect licensed premises through authorised officers|Examine samples and licence-related compliance|Take statutory action against violations where empowered','Licensing, seizure and prosecution require the applicable law and due process; this is not a hospital-treatment service.','A suspected substandard medicine can be sampled and examined through the authorised regulatory process.')
profile('health-financing','Administers eligibility, hospital coordination and claim-processing arrangements for the health-care programme assigned to the trust.', 'Publish or communicate scheme coverage and eligibility|Coordinate empanelled-hospital and authorisation workflows|Examine scheme claims and monitor programme performance','Treatment coverage and payment require the current scheme conditions and approval process.','An eligible treatment request is checked against scheme coverage and the prescribed authorisation requirements.')
profile('medical-infrastructure','Procures or develops the medical infrastructure, equipment and supplies assigned to the corporation.', 'Prepare and implement sanctioned health-infrastructure works|Conduct procurement through the applicable procedures|Monitor delivery, quality and maintenance arrangements','Procurement requires budget, approval and contract compliance; the corporation does not decide individual clinical treatment.','A sanctioned hospital-equipment requirement can be tendered, supplied and checked against the contract.')
profile('education-board','Administers the examinations, academic arrangements or institutional coordination assigned to the education board or council.', 'Issue approved academic or examination schedules|Conduct examinations and process results where assigned|Coordinate institutions and implement academic decisions within its remit','A board, directorate and university have different powers; the applicable education rules determine each decision.','An examination schedule is issued and eligible candidates are assessed through the prescribed examination process.')
profile('school-education','Administers assigned school-education services and programmes, including institutional support and monitoring.', 'Coordinate school operations and approved educational programmes|Monitor access, learning support and institutional requirements|Process staffing and programme proposals within delegated authority','Recognition, recruitment and student entitlements depend on the applicable rules and competent authority.','A school’s reported infrastructure need can be reviewed and proposed under an eligible education programme.')
profile('archives-library','Preserves documentary or published collections and provides the reading, reference and research services assigned to the institution.', 'Acquire, catalogue and preserve collections|Provide access or copies under the applicable access rules|Support research, exhibitions and public reading services','Access can be restricted by preservation requirements, privacy, copyright or archival rules.','A researcher can request access to an available record or publication through the institution’s access procedure.')
profile('police-command','Directs police operations and supervision for the force, commissionerate, district or specialist unit assigned to the command.', 'Deploy and supervise personnel within the assigned command|Coordinate crime prevention, investigation and public-order work|Review operational performance and complaints through the appropriate channels','Arrest, search, investigation and preventive orders require legal authority and procedure; police do not decide civil ownership or criminal guilt.','A reported series of offences can lead to a supervised investigation and deployment plan within the unit’s jurisdiction.')
profile('police-intelligence','Collects and assesses information for the security or intelligence responsibilities assigned to the unit.', 'Assess relevant threat and security information|Share intelligence with authorised operational authorities|Coordinate protective or preventive arrangements within its remit','Information gathering and operational action remain subject to legal authority and applicable safeguards.','A credible threat assessment can be shared with the police unit responsible for protective arrangements.')
profile('women-safety','Coordinates specialist police responses and prevention programmes concerning the safety of women within its assigned remit.', 'Route and monitor relevant complaints through authorised police units|Coordinate prevention, awareness and specialist support initiatives|Review investigation and response arrangements in the assigned cases','The unit’s role does not replace the criminal procedure, court process or the jurisdiction of the responsible station.','A safety complaint can be referred to the competent police team and followed up through the relevant support process.')
profile('police-recruitment','Conducts police-recruitment selection stages for posts notified under its assigned recruitment responsibilities.', 'Publish notified recruitment procedures and schedules|Organise eligibility checks, tests and selection stages|Publish results or selections under the applicable recruitment rules','A selection board cannot promise appointment outside a valid notification or bypass eligibility and reservation rules.','An applicant passes through the notified assessment stages for a police post.')
profile('anti-corruption','Investigates corruption offences involving public servants and other matters within the anti-corruption agency’s legal jurisdiction.', 'Receive and examine relevant corruption information|Conduct authorised inquiries and investigations|Submit investigation findings for the required prosecution process','Investigation and prosecution require the applicable legal permissions and procedure; a court determines criminal guilt.','A bribery complaint may be assessed and investigated by the authorised anti-corruption team.')
profile('cybercrime','Coordinates specialist policing for cybercrime and supports technical investigation and related prevention work.', 'Analyse cybercrime information and technical leads|Support or conduct investigations within assigned jurisdiction|Coordinate with financial and technical intermediaries through lawful requests','A reported loss does not guarantee recovery; account restraint and information access require the appropriate legal process.','Digital payment-fraud information can be examined and routed through authorised investigative and financial channels.')
profile('narcotics','Coordinates specialist enforcement and investigation concerning narcotic drugs and psychotropic substances within its notified remit.', 'Collect and assess relevant narcotics intelligence|Coordinate authorised investigations and enforcement operations|Support prevention and inter-agency case coordination','Search, seizure, arrest and prosecution are governed by the applicable narcotics and criminal-procedure law.','Intelligence about trafficking can be assessed and acted on by authorised officers through the statutory process.')
profile('special-police','Provides specialised armed, protective, counter-insurgency or counter-terrorism capability according to the unit’s assigned mandate.', 'Train and maintain specialist operational readiness|Deploy on authorised assignments|Coordinate with the territorial police and other competent units','A specialist unit’s name does not grant unlimited or statewide powers for every kind of case; the deployment order and law govern.','An authorised operation can draw on a trained specialist unit while local and senior commands coordinate responsibilities.')
profile('forensic-laboratory','Examines scientific evidence referred by authorised investigating agencies or courts and provides expert findings.', 'Receive and document referred exhibits|Perform relevant scientific examinations|Issue expert reports and provide evidence when required','An expert report supports the legal process; the laboratory does not decide guilt or pronounce a sentence.','A properly referred sample is examined and the results are supplied to the referring authority.')
profile('prisons','Administers custodial institutions and correctional services assigned to the prison department.', 'Manage lawful custody and institutional security|Arrange authorised welfare, rehabilitation and institutional services|Maintain custody records and implement court or competent-authority orders','Prison administration cannot impose a court sentence or independently alter a person’s judicial custody status.','A court remand order is implemented through the prison’s admission, record and custody procedures.')
profile('fire-disaster','Provides fire response, rescue and the fire-prevention or safety functions assigned to the service.', 'Dispatch authorised response teams and equipment|Conduct training, preparedness and safety inspections within its remit|Process fire-safety approvals where empowered','A fire-safety approval is separate from a building permit; each requires its own competent authority.','A fire incident prompts dispatch, rescue coordination and incident response by the relevant service.')
profile('printing','Provides the government printing, publication, stationery or related support services assigned to the department.', 'Prepare and print approved official material|Manage assigned stationery and supply arrangements|Maintain publication and distribution records','Printing an item does not create the policy or legal authority behind it.','An approved government notification can be prepared for the prescribed official publication process.')
profile('housing','Implements housing or residential-development projects assigned to the agency, including planning, construction and scheme administration.', 'Prepare and execute sanctioned housing projects|Process beneficiary or allotment matters under published rules|Monitor construction, contracts and project expenditure','A listing does not establish eligibility for a house; allotment and title follow the scheme and applicable approvals.','An approved housing project moves through beneficiary checks, sanctioned works and delivery monitoring.')
profile('industrial-facilitation','Supports industrial development and investment through the facilitation or infrastructure functions assigned to the agency.', 'Guide projects through relevant approval channels|Develop or manage industrial infrastructure where assigned|Monitor sanctioned industrial-development programmes','Facilitation does not replace the licences, environmental approvals or land permissions issued by competent authorities.','An industrial proposal can receive coordination support while its separate statutory applications are considered.')
profile('livelihood-enterprise','Supports the production, skills, marketing or livelihood development of the sector or producer group identified in its mandate.', 'Organise relevant training and enterprise support|Coordinate product development, procurement or marketing where assigned|Implement approved livelihood-development programmes','Support is governed by current programme and commercial terms; it is not a guaranteed market or income.','A producer group can receive training and assistance to reach an available marketing channel.')
profile('startup-support','Provides the incubation, entrepreneurship, prototyping, mentoring or ecosystem support identified in the organisation’s mandate.', 'Run announced startup or skill-development programmes|Connect participants with mentors, facilities or partner networks|Select and support eligible projects under programme terms','Participation does not guarantee investment, procurement, employment or regulatory approval.','An eligible team may enter a programme to test a prototype, develop skills or obtain mentoring.')
profile('digital-services','Supports government digital infrastructure or electronic delivery of public services through the functions assigned to the organisation.', 'Operate or support assigned technology platforms|Coordinate service integration, connectivity or technical procurement|Provide implementation and operational support to participating departments','The owning department remains responsible for the underlying service eligibility and official decision.','A department’s approved service can be integrated into a digital workflow while its authorised officer decides the application.')
profile('irrigation','Plans, develops or maintains the irrigation assets and command-area work assigned to the engineering organisation.', 'Survey and prepare technical proposals for assigned irrigation works|Execute sanctioned works and monitor quality|Operate or maintain allocated infrastructure and report its condition','Water release, procurement and expenditure approvals depend on the current allocation of powers and applicable orders.','An irrigation asset’s maintenance requirement is inspected, estimated and processed for the necessary sanction.')
profile('dam-safety','Coordinates dam-safety monitoring, technical assessment and compliance work within the organisation’s assigned statutory and engineering role.', 'Collect and review dam-condition and inspection information|Coordinate safety assessments and remedial recommendations|Monitor follow-up with the responsible dam-operating organisation','Safety oversight does not automatically make the office the operator of every dam or the authority for every water release.','An inspection finding can result in a technical recommendation and tracked remedial work by the responsible operator.')
profile('labour','Administers labour welfare, conciliation and compliance functions assigned to the labour organisation.', 'Receive and route employment-related complaints within jurisdiction|Conduct authorised inspection or conciliation proceedings|Implement assigned labour-welfare measures','The applicable labour law and forum determine enforceability; an administrative complaint is not automatically a court award.','An employment dispute can be examined for conciliation or referred to the competent adjudicatory forum.')
profile('employment-training','Provides employment facilitation, vocational training or placement-support services under its assigned programmes.', 'Register or guide eligible candidates under available services|Arrange training, job information and placement facilitation|Coordinate with employers and training providers','Registration or training does not guarantee a job or a particular salary.','A job seeker may be guided to a suitable notified training or employment opportunity.')
profile('factory-safety','Administers the industrial-safety, factory or boiler inspection functions identified in the organisation’s statutory mandate.', 'Examine required licence or certification applications|Inspect regulated workplaces or equipment through authorised officers|Issue statutory compliance action within delegated powers','Certification, inspection and enforcement must follow the relevant law and competent technical authorisation.','A regulated installation can be inspected against the conditions required for its statutory approval.')
profile('tribunal','Hears the classes of disputes or appeals assigned to this tribunal or specialist court by law.', 'Receive matters that meet filing and jurisdiction requirements|Conduct hearings and examine the material placed before it|Issue reasoned decisions or relief within its statutory powers','Jurisdiction and procedure vary by tribunal; the current constituting law and notified status must be checked.','A qualifying dispute is filed, heard and decided by the competent adjudicatory forum.')
profile('government-lawyer','Advises or represents the government in the legal work assigned to the law officer or counsel.', 'Prepare legal opinions and case submissions on instructions|Represent the government before the appropriate forum|Coordinate records and instructions with the concerned department','Government counsel advocates a position; the court decides the case. A counsel listing does not grant administrative control over the client department.','A department supplies case records and the assigned counsel prepares the government’s response to proceedings.')
profile('public-prosecution','Presents criminal prosecutions on behalf of the state through the prosecutor and court system.', 'Examine prosecution material and prepare the state’s submissions|Conduct assigned criminal proceedings in court|Coordinate with investigating officers on evidentiary and procedural requirements','Prosecutors do not independently pronounce guilt or replace the investigating agency; courts decide criminal cases.','An assigned prosecutor presents admissible evidence and legal submissions in a criminal trial.')
profile('waqf','Performs the waqf administration or oversight functions allocated to the board under the applicable legal framework.', 'Maintain and examine records within its assigned remit|Monitor administration of covered institutions and properties|Process matters through the competent statutory procedures','Current jurisdiction, property questions and remedies depend on applicable law and court orders; a directory entry is not proof of title.','An institution’s administration issue is examined against the relevant records and the procedure applicable to the board.')
profile('minorities-support','Provides the community-service, education, cultural or welfare support identified in the organisation’s mandate.', 'Organise announced services and support programmes|Coordinate eligible applications and participating institutions|Maintain programme records and communicate available assistance','Eligibility and services depend on current programme rules; the institution does not have general control over every community organisation.','An eligible applicant can seek information and assistance under a currently announced programme.')
profile('municipality','Provides local civic administration within its notified municipal area. Service responsibilities include local sanitation, streets and other municipal functions allocated by law.', 'Arrange sanitation and maintenance of assigned civic assets|Administer municipal revenues and applications through authorised officers|Plan and execute sanctioned local public works','Water supply, metropolitan planning, police and other agencies have separate responsibilities; municipal boundaries and delegated powers must be checked.','A street-light or sanitation complaint can be registered, assigned to the relevant municipal section and followed up.','https://ghmc.gov.in/CitizenCharter/CitizenCharter-19.06.pdf')
profile('urban-planning','Coordinates planned development and the land-use or planning functions assigned to the authority within its notified area.', 'Prepare or coordinate statutory plans and development proposals|Examine planning applications within its delegated jurisdiction|Implement sanctioned development and infrastructure projects','A planning authority is distinct from the municipal service provider; building, land-use and environmental approvals may involve different authorities.','A proposed layout is checked against the applicable plan and processed by the authority empowered to decide it.')
profile('water-board','Operates the water-supply and sewerage services assigned to the utility, including its network, connections and customer-service processes.', 'Operate and maintain allocated supply and sewerage infrastructure|Process eligible service connections and billing matters|Respond to reported service faults and maintain service records','Coverage depends on the utility’s notified service area; bulk-water and local network responsibilities may differ.','A water-supply fault is logged and referred to the network team responsible for the affected service area.')
profile('metro-infrastructure','Develops or coordinates metro-rail infrastructure and project arrangements assigned to the organisation.', 'Plan and coordinate approved metro-development work|Manage assigned project contracts and agency interfaces|Monitor project implementation and statutory clearances','The project agency and the train operator can be different organisations; a directory link does not establish who operates every service.','A sanctioned corridor component requires coordinated engineering, land and contractual approvals before construction.')
profile('rural-development','Coordinates rural-development programmes and the implementation systems assigned to the organisation.', 'Plan and monitor approved rural-development works|Coordinate field institutions, programme records and implementation support|Review eligible beneficiary and project proposals under programme rules','Local bodies retain their statutory functions; programme eligibility and sanctioning limits must be checked.','A sanctioned village development work is recorded, implemented and monitored through the relevant programme machinery.')
profile('rural-livelihoods','Works with community institutions and self-help groups to support livelihoods, access to services and eligible finance linkages.', 'Organise community mobilisation and capacity building|Facilitate eligible livelihood and bank-linkage proposals|Monitor approved community programmes and institutional support','Facilitation is not a guarantee of a bank loan, subsidy or household benefit.','A self-help group may obtain training and assistance in preparing an eligible livelihood-finance proposal.')
profile('statistics-gis','Produces or analyses official statistics, maps or geospatial information for planning and administrative decisions.', 'Collect, validate and analyse data within the assigned programme|Prepare statistical publications, maps or technical inputs|Support departments with relevant evidence and analytical services','A map or data product does not by itself settle legal title, statutory boundaries or an individual benefit claim.','A department can use a verified map layer or statistical series to plan and review a public programme.')
profile('land-administration','Coordinates land-revenue administration or the survey and land-record functions allocated to the office.', 'Maintain or supervise prescribed revenue and survey records|Process matters through the relevant revenue procedures|Review field-office performance and matters referred within its jurisdiction','Land-record entries, registration and judicial title disputes are distinct; only the competent authority can decide a particular proceeding.','A land-record discrepancy is examined against the applicable records and referred through the authorised correction or appeal process.')
profile('registration','Administers document registration and stamp-related services under the laws allocated to the department.', 'Receive and scrutinise registrable documents through authorised offices|Collect applicable duties and registration fees|Maintain registration records and provide permitted searches or certified services','Registration records a transaction under law; it is not an unrestricted government guarantee of ownership or freedom from every dispute.','A document is presented, checked for the prescribed requirements and registered by the competent registering officer.')
profile('excise','Administers the licensing, revenue and enforcement functions assigned under excise and prohibition law.', 'Process eligible licence applications through the prescribed authority|Inspect regulated activities and check compliance|Initiate statutory action against violations where authorised','Licence categories, permissions and penalties follow current policy and law; a directory title alone does not establish a sanctioning power.','An authorised inspection can identify a licence violation and lead to the prescribed compliance or enforcement process.')
profile('taxation','Administers the taxes assigned to the state tax organisation, including taxpayer services, compliance and enforcement.', 'Process registrations, returns and related taxpayer services|Conduct authorised assessment, audit or investigation|Issue notices or orders only through empowered officers and statutory procedure','Tax liability and remedies depend on the applicable legislation; taxpayers retain the prescribed response and appeal rights.','A discrepancy in a return may lead to a statutory notice and an opportunity to respond before a competent decision.')
profile('roads-buildings','Plans, builds or maintains the public roads and government buildings assigned to the engineering organisation.', 'Prepare surveys, designs and estimates for assigned works|Procure and supervise sanctioned construction or maintenance|Check quality and process measured contract work','Responsibility is limited to allocated assets; technical and financial approvals require the appropriate delegation.','A damaged stretch of an assigned road is inspected, estimated and taken through the maintenance approval process.')
profile('transport-regulation','Administers motor-vehicle regulation and transport services through authorised transport offices.', 'Process driving licences and vehicle registrations under the rules|Issue permits or fitness-related approvals through competent officers|Enforce vehicle and transport requirements through authorised staff','A transport office’s regulatory role is distinct from operating public buses; every application requires the prescribed eligibility and checks.','A driving-licence applicant completes the prescribed application and assessment process before the authorised office decides it.','https://www.telangana.gov.in/departments/transport/')
profile('bus-operator','Operates public bus services and manages the fleet, depots and passenger-service arrangements assigned to the corporation.', 'Plan available routes and service schedules|Operate and maintain buses and depots|Provide ticketing and handle passenger-service complaints','The bus corporation does not issue private driving licences or vehicle registrations; fares and service changes follow the relevant approvals.','A service reliability issue can be reviewed using depot, vehicle and scheduling information.')
profile('sports','Develops sports participation, coaching, facilities or athlete-support programmes within its assigned mandate.', 'Organise coaching and approved sporting activities|Operate or support allocated sports facilities|Process eligible athlete-development support under programme rules','Selection and assistance depend on sporting and programme criteria; participation does not guarantee employment or an award.','An eligible athlete may apply to an announced coaching or development programme.')
profile('women-child','Coordinates the women’s and children’s development services assigned to the organisation, including care, nutrition or protection-related programmes.', 'Implement approved care, nutrition and welfare services|Coordinate field institutions and relevant support agencies|Monitor eligible services and refer protection matters to competent authorities','Protection decisions, custody and criminal investigations belong to the authority empowered under the relevant law.','A reported service gap at a supported care centre can be examined and referred for corrective action.')
profile('food-nutrition','Produces or supplies the nutrition products assigned to the organisation for approved public programmes.', 'Plan production and procure inputs under approved procedures|Maintain food-quality controls and production records|Supply programme orders through the agreed distribution arrangements','It is a production and supply institution; beneficiary eligibility and clinical nutrition advice are separate responsibilities.','A nutrition-programme supply order is manufactured, quality checked and dispatched to the prescribed delivery point.')
profile('culture-heritage','Preserves or promotes the heritage, language, literature, arts or museum functions identified in the institution’s mandate.', 'Organise relevant conservation, collection or cultural programmes|Document and support practitioners, works or collections|Provide public access, exhibitions or learning activities as assigned','Protected-site permissions, funding and collection access require the applicable rules and competent authority.','An exhibition or cultural programme can be prepared using the institution’s approved collections and programme budget.')
profile('tourism','Develops or operates the tourism facilities and visitor services assigned to the organisation.', 'Operate available tourism properties or services|Develop sanctioned visitor infrastructure|Promote destinations and coordinate tourism programmes','Service availability follows current operating terms; the agency does not issue every travel or protected-site permission.','A visitor can use an available service while the corporation maintains and markets the relevant tourism facility.')
profile('public-communication','Provides official public communication, media coordination or professional media-support services within its assigned mandate.', 'Prepare and distribute authorised public information|Coordinate relevant media or communication programmes|Organise training or outreach where assigned','Communicating an announcement does not create the scheme entitlement or confer executive authority over another department.','An approved programme announcement is explained through a public-information release or outreach activity.')
profile('public-service-commission','Conducts recruitment examinations for the state services assigned to the commission and provides service-related advice where constitutionally required.', 'Issue recruitment notifications and conduct the prescribed selection stages|Publish results and recommend candidates under the applicable rules|Provide advice on referred service matters within Article 320 and applicable exemptions','Recommendations and selection stages are different from the appointing department’s appointment order; the commission cannot bypass a valid recruitment rule.','After a valid recruitment notification, eligible candidates complete the selection stages and recommendations are sent through the prescribed process.','https://www.upsc.gov.in/about-us/constitutional-provisions/article-320-functions-public-service-commissions')
profile('election-commission','Supervises elections to the local bodies placed under the State Election Commission’s constitutional and statutory remit.', 'Direct preparation of the relevant local-body electoral rolls|Schedule and supervise covered local-body elections|Issue election instructions within its legal powers','Assembly and Parliamentary elections fall under the Election Commission of India, rather than this local-body commission.','A notified local-body election is conducted through the election officers and procedures supervised by the commission.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('finance-commission','Reviews the finances of local bodies and makes recommendations on the distribution of financial resources under its constitutional remit.', 'Examine local-body revenue and expenditure information|Consult relevant institutions and assess financial needs|Submit recommendations on resource sharing and related matters','It recommends a financial framework; it does not itself approve each municipal bill or automatically release a grant.','Local-body finance evidence is assessed and used in a report recommending how resources should be distributed.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('rights-commission','Examines the complaints, safeguards and policy issues assigned to the rights commission under its governing law.', 'Receive and examine matters within its jurisdiction|Seek information and undertake inquiries where legally empowered|Make findings or recommendations and monitor responses as the law permits','A commission’s recommendations and inquiry powers differ from a court’s sentencing powers; its own governing law controls each remedy.','An admissible complaint can lead to an inquiry and recommendations to the responsible authority.')
profile('lokayukta','Examines allegations against covered public functionaries through the complaints and investigation process assigned to the Lokayukta institution.', 'Scrutinise admissible complaints under the governing Act|Conduct or arrange inquiries within jurisdiction|Report findings and recommendations through the statutory process','It is not a substitute for every service grievance or civil appeal; jurisdiction, exclusions and remedies follow the applicable Act.','A complaint within the institution’s jurisdiction can be examined and findings communicated to the competent authority.','https://lokayukta.telangana.gov.in/files/Annual-Reports-2024.pdf')
profile('vigilance','Examines administrative integrity, misconduct or irregularity matters allocated to the vigilance organisation.', 'Seek records and examine referred irregularities|Coordinate inspections or inquiries within its remit|Report findings and recommend appropriate follow-up','Vigilance advice, departmental discipline and criminal investigation are separate processes with different competent authorities.','A referred irregularity may lead to a records-based examination and recommendations for departmental or other appropriate action.')
profile('legal-aid','Coordinates the legal-aid and access-to-justice functions assigned to the legal-services authority.', 'Organise eligible legal aid and advice|Support Lok Adalat and legal-awareness activities under the applicable framework|Coordinate participating legal-services institutions','Legal aid eligibility and a dispute’s suitability for settlement follow the applicable rules; the authority does not guarantee a particular case outcome.','An eligible applicant can be assessed for legal assistance and referred to the appropriate service.')
profile('fee-regulation','Examines fee proposals and related matters for the institutions and courses covered by the fee-regulatory framework.', 'Seek relevant fee and institutional information|Examine proposals through the prescribed process|Make or communicate fee recommendations or determinations within its notified powers','Coverage and the final fee-notification process depend on the governing rules; it does not regulate every private educational charge.','An institution’s covered fee proposal is assessed using the financial and academic information required by the applicable framework.')
profile('disaster-relief','Coordinates the preparedness, relief, recovery or rehabilitation work specifically allocated to the office.', 'Compile field information and coordinate relevant agencies|Process eligible relief or rehabilitation proposals|Monitor sanctioned assistance and assigned response work','Assistance requires the applicable notification and eligibility; coordination does not grant every agency’s operational powers.','A district impact report can be assessed and routed for the relief measures available under the applicable government orders.')
profile('translation','Provides the official language translation and linguistic support work assigned to the office.', 'Translate referred government material|Check terminology and consistency in assigned documents|Maintain and supply approved translations through the prescribed process','A translation service does not decide the underlying policy or alter a legal text’s authoritative status.','A referred government document is translated and checked before being returned for the required official use.')
profile('estate','Administers the government accommodation, premises or property-management work assigned to the estate office.', 'Maintain assigned property and occupancy records|Process accommodation or estate-service matters under the rules|Coordinate maintenance and compliance with relevant agencies','Allotment, eviction and property decisions require the competent authority and applicable legal procedure.','An office accommodation request can be checked against availability and the applicable allotment rules.')
profile('sainik','Supports the welfare and resettlement services assigned for ex-service personnel, dependants and eligible beneficiaries.', 'Provide information and eligibility guidance|Process applications for available welfare measures|Coordinate with service and district welfare institutions','Benefits and certification depend on the relevant scheme and authorised records.','An eligible dependant can seek guidance on the documents and process required for an available welfare benefit.')
profile('publication-registration','Administers the publication-related records and functions allocated to the Registrar of Publications in the government staffing framework.', 'Maintain the publication records assigned to the office|Process referred publication-related administrative work|Provide information through the office’s authorised procedures','The staffing register does not establish a newspaper licensing or censorship power; the office’s current duty allocation must be checked.','A publication-related administrative query can be referred to the office for confirmation of its current remit.')
profile('rain-shadow','Appears as a retained departmental heading in the 2026–27 staffing register. That budget listing alone does not establish the office’s current operational programmes.', 'Identify the listed office and its budget-sector association|Refer a query about its current work to the responsible department|Use a current work-allocation order to establish any specific decision-making power','No active scheme, field jurisdiction or sanctioning power is inferred from the register entry.','A reader checking a rain-shadow development function should obtain the current departmental allocation before treating this heading as the implementing agency.')
# Leadership, representation and staff roles. Institution powers are deliberately not
# inherited by an individual member, adviser, support officer or engineering employee.
profile('chief-minister','Heads the Council of Ministers and gives political direction to the elected state government. Departmental decisions are processed through the state’s business rules and the competent minister, Cabinet or authorised official.', 'Set government priorities and coordinate ministerial policy|Lead Cabinet consideration of matters requiring a collective decision|Review the portfolios held by the CM and communicate constitutionally required information to the Governor','The CM does not exercise the judicial powers of courts or the independent statutory powers of every commission.','A proposal involving several departments can be coordinated and placed through the required government decision process.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('minister','Provides political leadership for the portfolios allocated to the minister. The department’s civil-service leadership prepares proposals, administers programmes and carries out authorised decisions.', 'Review policy proposals and programme performance in allocated subjects|Take decisions that fall within the minister’s authorised business allocation|Present or answer for portfolio business in the Legislature','The title does not place every state agency or another minister under this office; Cabinet, financial and legal approvals may still be needed.','A proposal for a new portfolio programme is reviewed and routed for the financial, Cabinet or legislative approvals it requires.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('cabinet','The Council of Ministers provides the state’s collective political executive under the Chief Minister. Ministers are collectively responsible to the Legislative Assembly.', 'Consider matters placed before the Council under government business rules|Agree collective policy and legislative proposals|Coordinate decisions requiring more than one portfolio','A Cabinet decision still needs the applicable legal authority, appropriation and implementation orders.','A major cross-department proposal can be considered collectively before the responsible departments implement the authorised decision.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('chief-secretary','Coordinates the senior civil administration and helps departments implement government decisions. This is administrative leadership within the executive, rather than an elected or judicial office.', 'Convene interdepartmental reviews and resolve administrative coordination issues|Review implementation and escalate matters requiring government decisions|Process the administrative matters allocated to the office','The office cannot replace a court or bypass a power reserved to a minister, statutory body or other competent authority.','When a programme needs several departments, the Chief Secretary can coordinate responsibilities and review implementation milestones.')
profile('governor','Serves as the state’s constitutional head. Executive, legislative and other functions operate within constitutional provisions, ordinarily on the aid and advice of the Council of Ministers, with constitutionally recognised exceptions.', 'Appoint the Chief Minister and ministers under the constitutional process|Summon or prorogue the Legislature and consider Bills as provided by the Constitution|Perform other constitutional functions in the circumstances and manner permitted','The Governor is not the day-to-day manager of every government department; discretion is governed by the Constitution and applicable judicial interpretation.','After a Bill is passed, it is presented for the Governor’s consideration under the constitutional procedure.','https://governor.telangana.gov.in/roleofgovernor.do')
profile('mla','Represents an Assembly constituency in the state’s directly elected House. Lawmaking, public-finance approval and scrutiny of ministers are core responsibilities; constituency representation connects local concerns with those processes.', 'Debate and vote on Bills and Assembly financial business|Ask questions and raise public or constituency issues using House procedures|Participate in committees when appointed and make representations to authorities','An MLA does not personally issue land titles, appoint government staff, direct a court or automatically control district officers.','A local service problem can be raised with the responsible department and, where permitted, through an Assembly question.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('mlc','Serves in the Legislative Council, the state Legislature’s upper chamber. The Council examines legislation and public issues through its constitutionally defined powers and House procedures.', 'Debate Bills and participate in Council proceedings|Ask questions and raise matters under Council rules|Serve on committees when appointed','The Council’s powers differ from the Assembly’s, particularly for Money Bills and financial control; an MLC is not a district administrator.','A member can question a department’s programme performance and contribute to examination of a Bill.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('mp','Participates in India’s Parliament on national legislation, Union finances and scrutiny of the Union government. The elected or chosen House determines the member’s procedural and financial powers.', 'Debate national Bills and vote where the member’s House has the relevant power|Use questions and permitted parliamentary procedures to raise issues|Participate in parliamentary committees when appointed','An MP is separate from the state’s executive chain and does not directly sanction every state service or command district officials.','An issue requiring Union government action can be raised through a parliamentary question or representation to the responsible ministry.','https://sansad.in/ls/committee/introduction')
profile('speaker','Presides over the Legislative Assembly and is responsible for conducting proceedings according to constitutional provisions and House rules.', 'Regulate debates and maintain order during sittings|Apply procedural rules and decide matters assigned to the presiding officer|Perform constitutionally assigned functions, including Money Bill certification where applicable','The presiding office is distinct from executive government; its decisions remain subject to the applicable constitutional framework.','During a sitting, the Speaker determines whether a procedural intervention is admissible under the House rules.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('council-chair','Presides over the Legislative Council and conducts its business according to the Constitution and Council rules.', 'Regulate Council debates and maintain order|Apply the Council’s rules of procedure|Perform procedural functions allocated to the Chairman','The Chairman does not acquire the Assembly Speaker’s separate Money Bill certification power or executive control over departments.','A procedural issue arising during a Council debate is decided under the Council’s rules.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('high-court','Exercises judicial functions independently of the state’s political executive. The High Court hears matters within its original, appellate and constitutional jurisdiction through duly constituted benches.', 'Hear and decide matters within the Court’s jurisdiction|Issue writs and other judicial orders where the law permits|Exercise the supervisory and administrative functions constitutionally assigned to the Court','A case must meet jurisdictional and procedural requirements; an individual directory listing does not establish which bench will hear it.','A qualifying challenge to unlawful public action can be brought before the Court for a judicial decision.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('chief-justice','Heads the High Court and exercises judicial functions as a judge, alongside the administrative responsibilities assigned to the Chief Justice.', 'Hear matters assigned to the bench on which the Chief Justice sits|Constitute benches and allocate judicial work through the roster|Lead court administration within the constitutional and statutory framework','Other judges decide their assigned cases judicially; administrative leadership does not mean deciding every case personally.','The roster allocates categories of cases to benches, which then hear and decide those matters independently.',CONSTITUTION)
profile('court-registry','Supports the Court’s case administration or institutional management in the section identified by the designation.', 'Scrutinise and process filings or administrative matters in the assigned section|Maintain records and communicate authorised court notices or orders|Place procedural or administrative matters before the competent authority','A Registrar’s administrative role does not automatically include deciding the merits of a case; any judicial powers require a specific legal assignment.','A filing defect can be communicated so a party can correct it before the matter progresses under the Court’s rules.')
profile('information-commission','Decides state-public-authority RTI second appeals and examines complaints through the distinct procedures provided by the RTI Act. It concerns access to information, rather than general redress of the underlying service grievance.', 'Hear second appeals under section 19 and complaints under section 18|Direct appropriate disclosure or compliance measures in appeal proceedings within statutory powers|Consider penalties or disciplinary recommendations under section 20 after the required process','Information exemptions and statutory procedures apply; an RTI proceeding does not itself decide property title, award a government job or resolve every service dispute.','A person denied requested public information can use the applicable appeal route, and the commission can examine the information-access dispute.','https://www.indiacode.nic.in/bitstream/123456789/2065/5/a2005-22.pdf')
profile('collector','Leads the district’s civil and revenue administration and coordinates delivery of government programmes. Collector, District Magistrate and election-related responsibilities depend on the statutory appointments and work allocated to the officer.', 'Review district programme delivery and coordinate departmental responses|Hear or process revenue matters where legally empowered|Coordinate assigned disaster-response and district administrative work','Police command, judicial decisions and approvals reserved to another authority remain separate; a Collector cannot unilaterally settle every land-title dispute.','A district-level service issue can be reviewed with the concerned field departments and followed through the appropriate administrative process.','https://hyderabad.telangana.gov.in/collectrate/')
profile('additional-collector','Assists district administration in the charge allocated to this particular post. Revenue and local-body assignments are different, and the current allocation determines which files and programmes this officer handles.', 'Review matters and field-office progress in the assigned charge|Hear, process or decide cases only where a specific delegation permits|Coordinate follow-up and submit matters requiring the Collector or another authority','The designation alone does not confirm the current revenue, local-body or other charge.','An allocated revenue or local-body matter can be examined and either decided within delegation or submitted to the competent authority.')
profile('secretariat-officer','Processes government policy and administrative business in the subjects allocated to this Secretariat post. Work typically moves from examination and consultation to approval, orders and implementation review.', 'Examine proposals, record advice and obtain required departmental views|Submit matters to the minister, Cabinet or other competent authority|Issue or authenticate approved communications and monitor assigned implementation where authorised','A Secretary, Joint Secretary and Deputy Secretary have different delegations; the listing does not establish unlimited policy, financial or statutory powers.','A field agency’s proposal is examined for policy, finance and legal issues before being placed at the correct approval level.')
profile('cmo-officer','Supports the Chief Minister’s office in the correspondence, briefing, scheduling or coordination responsibilities allocated to the post.', 'Prepare assigned briefs and process official correspondence|Seek or coordinate departmental inputs on referred matters|Track follow-up on authorised directions','A CMO posting does not automatically transfer a department’s statutory decision-making powers to the officer.','A representation sent to the CMO can be referred to the competent department and its response tracked.')
profile('adviser','Provides subject-specific advice and recommendations in the area allocated to the advisory appointment. An adviser’s contribution informs decisions made by the competent executive or statutory authority.', 'Review referred proposals and offer subject advice|Recommend options or improvements|Participate in assigned consultations and reviews','Advisory status alone does not confer authority to issue binding departmental orders, sanction expenditure or appoint staff.','A policy proposal may be referred for advice before the responsible department seeks a formal decision.')
profile('chair','Leads the board, commission, committee or governing body in the capacity assigned by its constituting rules. Collective governance is different from the organisation’s daily executive management.', 'Convene or preside over governing-body meetings where assigned|Guide consideration of strategy, performance and governance issues|Participate in decisions according to the body’s rules','A chairperson is not automatically the chief executive or sole decision-maker; statutory adjudicatory powers require the relevant legal appointment.','A major institutional proposal can be considered at a properly constituted board meeting.')
profile('board-member','Participates in the governing or specialist body in the capacity specified by the appointment, such as technical, financial or other membership.', 'Examine papers and contribute relevant expertise|Participate in deliberations and votes where the rules permit|Follow up on responsibilities formally allocated to the member','Membership alone does not authorise issuing orders on behalf of the entire institution or exercising its staff’s statutory powers.','A technical member may scrutinise the technical aspects of a proposal before the body reaches a decision.')
profile('chief-executive','Manages the organisation’s operations and implements the decisions allocated to its executive leadership. The board, government and statutory authorities can retain separate approval powers.', 'Coordinate operating plans, staff and service delivery|Manage contracts, resources and expenditure within delegated limits|Submit major policy, investment or governance matters for the required approval','An MD, CEO or CMD is bound by the organisation’s governing framework and financial delegation; the title does not authorise every licence or regulatory action.','A sanctioned project is translated into operating assignments, procurement steps and progress reviews.')
profile('directorate-officer','Directs or supports the programme and administrative functions allocated to this directorate or specialist post. The subject in the designation and the parent organisation define the practical area of work.', 'Plan and review activities in the assigned subject|Process operational, staffing or programme proposals within delegation|Monitor field or institutional delivery and escalate matters requiring higher approval','Director, Additional Director and Joint Director posts have different assignments; statutory or financial sanctions require the relevant authorisation.','A programme implementation issue can be reviewed, corrective action assigned and any reserved decision referred to the competent authority.')
profile('engineer','Provides engineering planning, technical scrutiny, execution or maintenance in the organisation and discipline identified by the post.', 'Prepare or examine surveys, designs and estimates within the assigned technical charge|Supervise sanctioned works, check quality and review progress|Certify measurements or make technical recommendations only within the assigned delegation','Chief, Superintending, Executive and Assistant Engineers have different powers; technical review is separate from administrative sanction and procurement approval.','A proposed repair is inspected and estimated, then taken through the technical and financial approvals required before execution.')
profile('finance-officer','Handles the organisation’s assigned financial advice, budgeting, accounts or payment-control function.', 'Examine financial proposals and budget availability|Maintain or review accounts, bills and reconciliations|Flag financial-rule issues and submit matters requiring the competent sanction','Checking a bill or providing financial advice does not create authority to spend beyond a valid sanction and delegation.','A purchase proposal is checked against the approved budget and financial rules before the competent authority decides it.')
profile('company-secretary','Supports the company’s corporate governance, board process and statutory corporate-compliance work.', 'Arrange board or committee papers and maintain required corporate records|Coordinate statutory filings and compliance reporting|Advise on corporate procedural requirements within the assigned remit','A Company Secretary is different from a Secretary to Government and does not hold general government policy or judicial powers.','A board-approved corporate matter is documented and the required statutory filing is arranged.')
profile('registrar','Administers the registration, academic-record, membership or institutional process allocated to this Registrar post. The parent organisation determines which of those functions applies.', 'Maintain the records and process the cases allocated to the Registrar|Scrutinise applications or institutional matters under the relevant rules|Issue authorised communications and refer reserved decisions to the competent authority','A university, co-operative and court Registrar have different powers; the title alone does not establish a court or society-registration jurisdiction.','An application can be checked against the parent institution’s rules and routed to the authority empowered to decide it.')
profile('section-officer','Supervises the processing of work in an office section, including files, records, drafts and follow-up.', 'Allocate and check section work and file completeness|Prepare or review notes, drafts and administrative records|Track pending cases and place decision-ready matters before the authorised officer','Section supervision does not by itself confer power to approve a scheme, impose a penalty or sanction expenditure.','A representation is diarised, relevant records are obtained and a checked note is submitted for a decision.')
profile('personal-support','Provides the correspondence, scheduling, documentation or executive-support work allocated to the person’s attached office.', 'Manage authorised appointments and correspondence|Prepare records, briefs or communications as assigned|Coordinate meetings and follow-up with the relevant office','A personal assistant or private secretary does not acquire the statutory or financial powers of the official they support.','Meeting material is collected and an authorised appointment or follow-up communication is arranged.')
profile('project-officer','Coordinates the implementation and monitoring of the particular project or programme allocated to the post.', 'Prepare work plans and coordinate assigned implementation|Monitor field progress, records and expenditure against sanctioned activities|Submit issues and proposals requiring the programme’s competent authority','The project’s rules and written delegation determine approval powers; the title does not establish control over unrelated programmes.','A delayed project activity is reviewed and an implementation issue is referred to the responsible team or sanctioning authority.')
profile('manager','Manages an allocated operational, regional or functional unit within the organisation. The designation’s subject and current assignment define the service or business responsibilities.', 'Coordinate day-to-day work and staff in the assigned unit|Review service performance, records and operational needs|Process resources and decisions within the authorised delegation','A manager is not automatically a regulator or the organisation’s final sanctioning authority.','An operational service problem is investigated and resolved within the unit’s authority or escalated with supporting records.')
profile('specialist-support','Provides the professional or administrative function named in the designation for the listed organisation. The directory identifies the post but does not publish a complete individual duty or delegation order.', 'Examine and prepare the technical or administrative work assigned to the post|Maintain relevant records and coordinate with the responsible section|Submit advice or proposals to the officer authorised to decide','No licensing, enforcement, recruitment or financial sanction is inferred solely from this directory title; the current written assignment is needed for an exact power.','An assigned matter is examined within the post’s professional remit and placed before the competent decision-maker.')
HYDRAA='https://hydraa.telangana.gov.in/about'
profile('hydraa','Combines urban disaster management and protection of public assets within the notified CURE region. Its operational work is organised through specialist wings under the Commissioner.', 'Coordinate protection of lakes, nalas, parks and government land|Organise preparedness, rescue and inter-agency response|Carry out authorised enforcement with the competent authorities','Its remit is the notified CURE area. Notices, removal or criminal action require the relevant legal authority and procedure.','A public-asset report can be examined and referred for the relevant verification and authorised response.',HYDRAA)
profile('hydraa-commissioner','Leads HYDRAA’s administration and operations under MA&UD supervision and coordinates its wings. The agency profile also identifies the Commissioner as chair of the Lake Protection Committee.', 'Coordinate wing priorities and operational reviews|Convene or participate in assigned asset-protection coordination|Oversee resources and matters delegated to the Commissioner','Agency leadership does not remove statutory safeguards or transfer every municipality’s powers to the Commissioner.','A matter involving several wings can be coordinated through the Commissioner’s office.',HYDRAA)
profile('hydraa-assets','Carries out HYDRAA’s asset-protection and restoration work for public land, lakes, parks and open spaces in its notified remit.', 'Verify reported encroachments with relevant records and agencies|Plan authorised protection, restoration and enforcement work|Track compliance and coordinate follow-up','Land status, notices and enforcement authority must be established; a complaint alone does not prove an encroachment.','A reported obstruction is checked before the competent authority decides the permitted response.','https://hydraa.telangana.gov.in/functions/asset-protection')
profile('hydraa-disaster','Coordinates HYDRAA’s disaster-preparedness and response capability, including rescue arrangements and flood-related coordination.', 'Plan and coordinate emergency response and rescue|Organise preparedness exercises and community awareness|Coordinate field resources and relevant agencies during an incident','Operational deployment follows the notified remit, incident responsibilities and applicable safety requirements.','During severe rainfall, response teams and supporting agencies coordinate rescue and incident information.','https://hydraa.telangana.gov.in/functions/disaster-management')
profile('hydraa-logistics','Provides the people, equipment, fleet, communications and technical systems needed for HYDRAA’s operational readiness.', 'Manage assigned personnel, equipment and fleet support|Support IT, GIS and the disaster-information system|Coordinate training, resources and field logistics','Support responsibilities do not themselves confer powers to decide land title or impose criminal punishment.','An operational team receives the vehicles, communications and mapped information needed for its assignment.','https://hydraa.telangana.gov.in/functions/logistics')
profile('hydraa-station','Provides the criminal-enforcement branch identified in HYDRAA’s published structure. Police work remains governed by the applicable criminal law and notified jurisdiction.', 'Receive and examine matters within the station’s notified remit|Investigate cognisable offences through authorised officers and lawful procedure|Coordinate with agency wings and other police units','The station does not decide civil title or criminal guilt. Exact station jurisdiction and assigned offences require the relevant notification.','An agency matter involving an alleged criminal offence can be referred for the appropriate police examination.',HYDRAA)
profile('ground-water','Studies groundwater resources and provides the technical assessment, monitoring and advice assigned to the department.', 'Monitor groundwater conditions and analyse available observations|Carry out hydrogeological surveys and technical studies|Provide technical inputs for water-resource planning and referred proposals','A technical assessment does not itself confer land rights or every permission needed to drill or extract water.','A proposed water-supply source can be assessed using groundwater observations and a relevant technical survey.')
profile('civil-defence','Supports civilian preparedness and protection through the training, volunteer and coordination functions assigned to civil defence.', 'Organise authorised volunteer training and preparedness activities|Support awareness and emergency coordination arrangements|Mobilise assigned support resources through the competent command','Civil-defence support does not automatically include the powers of police, fire services or a district magistrate.','Trained volunteers can assist an authorised preparedness exercise or emergency-support operation.')
profile('command-centre','Supports police and other authorised public-safety operations through shared information, communications and command-centre coordination.', 'Receive and organise operational information within authorised systems|Coordinate communication between participating units|Provide situational information to the responsible decision-makers','Access to data and operational action require lawful authorisation; a command centre is not a court or a universal complaint-deciding body.','During a major incident, relevant information can be brought together so the responsible field commands coordinate their response.')
profile('broadcast-education','Provides educational broadcasting and digital learning content through the channels and programmes assigned to T-SAT / SoFTNET.', 'Produce or schedule educational programmes|Broadcast or distribute approved learning content|Coordinate subject inputs with participating institutions','Watching a programme does not itself confer a recognised qualification or guarantee examination success.','A learner can use a scheduled lesson or examination-preparation programme as supplementary study support.')

